{"c":[{"id":"cc86c50101fc2328","sum":"T2: en_AU accepts 'seperate'/'truely', so NativeChecker uses US/GB/CA witnesses; NSSpellChecker may autocorrect to its 2nd guess (adress->dress). H4: build-app.sh holds build.lock all run; callers under heavy.sh/lockf set CARET_NO_LOCK=1; release/acceptance need IDENTITY.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T212904Z-f841172a94ee81e8","text":"T2: macOS 26.6's en_AU spell dictionary accepts 'seperate' and 'truely'; NativeChecker uses US/GB/CA as regional witnesses and en-AU only when the user lists it. In context NSSpellChecker can autocorrect to its 2nd guess ('adress' -> dress while guess 1 is address).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T220029Z-2e8d5e2431d5ac81","text":"H4: build-app.sh takes build.lock for the whole run (compile, copy, sign); a caller already under heavy.sh or lockf sets CARET_NO_LOCK=1 or it deadlocks. release and acceptance need IDENTITY (team cert SHA-1); debug is ad hoc.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0b2cc0daa10616a1","sum":"H4: SIP is off on Sam's Mac, so hardened runtime/library validation aren't enforced; measure entitlements on a SIP-on Mac. A built Caret.app starts its own helper and reader unless --helper-socket or CARET_SCREEN_SOCKET names one; test runs pass --home DIR.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T220029Z-8a608f67782b76c4","text":"H4: SIP is disabled on Sam's Mac (csrutil status), so the hardened runtime and library validation are not enforced there; node.entitlements (allow-jit only) and any entitlement question must be measured on a SIP-on Mac.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T220029Z-91a1d68b9a61d85a","text":"H4: a built Caret.app starts its own helper and reader unless --helper-socket or CARET_SCREEN_SOCKET names one; test runs of a bundle pass --home DIR (sockets, data, host.sock and settings move there) and never run with neither.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
